{"diagnosis": "Loopback UART via simpleuart at picosoc/picosoc.v:190 (module at picosoc/simpleuart.v:20) trapped `TRAP: uart data mismatch got 0xf0 want 0xa5` with tohost `FAIL 0xdead`. TX `ser_tx` should idle high but excerpt line 131 shifts `{1'b0, send_pattern[9:1]}` pulling the line low after dummy/data frames. The low idle creates a false start and misaligned sampling in loopback, corrupting 0xa5 to 0xf0.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -128,7 +128,7 @@
 				send_divcnt <= 0;
 			end else
 			if (send_divcnt > cfg_divider && send_bitcnt) begin
-				send_pattern <= {1'b0, send_pattern[9:1]};
+				send_pattern <= {1'b1, send_pattern[9:1]};
 				send_bitcnt <= send_bitcnt - 1;
 				send_divcnt <= 0;
 			end
", "expected": "tohost PASS (no TRAP), uart loopback got 0xa5 want 0xa5, checksum != 7f1f8653d81beffbf56c64348d4b664a9ffa3b217fbca29ca6a0e86da0c3cbf9"}

